    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is anchored today by **Lawrence Butler**, who represents our strongest play with a 73.47 efficiency score. His matchup against Peralta is highly favorable, bolstered by a significant 13% boost from his platoon advantage and a 10% park factor bump. Similarly, **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65) and **Jonathan Aranda** (65.13) occupy the top of the order with high confidence scores, as both benefit from elite situational positioning and advantageous xERA matchups against Wesneski and Lopez, respectively. **Bryce Harper** remains a steady, high-ceiling play at 61.71; while he faces Dobbins, his elite xwOBA metrics and favorable spot in the three-hole ensure he stays in the daily rotation to maximize our counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today involved **Gavin Sheets**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 38.33 score. While his platoon edge against Henderson provided a lift, the opposing xERA of 2.82 acted as a severe anchor, plummeting his SP Skill contribution by 19% and dropping him below our \"Zebras Floor\" of 40.0. Consequently, we are prioritizing the higher-upside profiles of **Dylan Beavers** and **Justin Crawford** in the outfield to chase the scarce stolen base production we desperately need in this 5x5 format. \n\nRisks for the slate are relatively contained, though we remain vigilant regarding the bottom of our order. Both **Zack Gelof** and **Kyle Karros** are hovering near our bench threshold, and any late-breaking news regarding lineup shifts\u2014specifically for **Masyn Winn** or **Daulton Varsho**\u2014could force a pivot to the bench. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, and **Tyler Freeman**, as their absence from the active roster continues to limit our flexibility. We are also keeping an eye on whether **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Brendan Donovan**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Alex Freeland**, or **Braden Montgomery** see any pinch-hit availability if the game scripts turn stagnant. **Yainer Diaz** remains a key piece we are tracking for potential promotion from the bench if mid-day injury reports emerge.",
